  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1208 PM CDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nDepending on the location of the frontal boundary from Wednesday, \nprecipitation chances could continue into Thursday. Models indicate \nthe boundary will push farther through the forecast area through the \nday Tuesday bringing widespread chances for storms. Similar to \nWednesday, severe thunderstorms are not expected Thursday. With \nprecipitation chances and mostly cloudy skies through the day, \ntemperatures will slighlty cool to the lower 90s across much of the \nregion. Areas across the southern Rolling Plains will see highs in \nthe upper 90s. Sadly, temperatures warm back up to the upper 90s and \nlower triple digits over the weekend. The persistent upper ridging \nwill retreat west through the latter half of the week. Precipitation \nchances return midway through the weekend and continue through early \nnext week as the upper ridging parks over the Desert Southwest \nbringing northwesterly flow aloft. Daily precipitation chances will \nslightly cool temperatures early next week back to the 90s across \nthe region. Some lucky areas on the Caprock may see highs in the \nupper 80s!",
